  "limitations": [
    "HomeReady is the actual Home data/layout loading boundary, not physical frame presentation.",
    "Process-cold preserves account data and warm OS/filesystem caches; no fully uncached or populated-list qualification.",
    "Native HOT resumes do not establish authoritative refreshed-data readiness or the warm usable-screen target.",
    "Transport starts at fetch and ends at Response; auth acquisition, JSON decoding and local projection are excluded.",
    "Content-Length values are metadata, not measured wire bytes.",
    "Fixed six-second screen smoke observations are not screen-transition/data-ready latency.",
    "No p99, concurrency, writes, provider work or paired speedup claim."
  ]
